    {
      "tag": "main",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "h1",
          "children": [
            "Foundations and reproducible SQL"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "children": [
            "Use PostgreSQL 16+ and a dedicated empty teaching database. These exercises support meetings 1, 2, and 5. Start with ",
            {
              "tag": "a",
              "attrs": {
                "href": "setup.sql"
              },
              "children": [
                "setup.sql"
              ]
            },
            "; it creates only the ",
            {
              "tag": "code",
              "children": [
                "course32"
              ]
            },
            " schema and deliberately fails if that schema already exists. For a repeat run, create a fresh teaching database instead of dropping existing work."
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "children": [
            "Meeting 1: requirements before syntax"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "children": [
            "A campus currently keeps event registrations in separate spreadsheets. Two staff members can edit seats remaining; a student may register twice; event titles are copied into every row. In pairs, identify three inconsistent states and assign each to a key, foreign key, transaction, or application rule. Explain what a DBMS can enforce and what still requires a precise requirement."
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "children": [
            "Meeting 2: setup and integrity lab"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "children": [
            "Budget: 10 minutes predictions, 15 setup demonstration, 15 guided constraints, 50 independent work, 10 debrief."
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "ol",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Run setup.sql. Verify 5 students, 4 events, 6 bookings, and total account balance 200.00."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Display student names alphabetically; display events with fee at least 20; return event titles and capacity only."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "In separate BEGIN/ROLLBACK blocks, try a duplicate student ID, a booking for student 999, fee -1, and a NULL student name. Record the constraint responsible. After an error issue ROLLBACK before the next test."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Choose types for money, event dates, email, and capacity. Explain why numeric money and integer capacity express different domains."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Add one valid student and booking in a transaction, inspect them, then roll back. Verify original counts."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "children": [
            "Meeting 5: query exercises"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "ol",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Find students without email. Explain why ",
                {
                  "tag": "code",
                  "children": [
                    "email = NULL"
                  ]
                },
                " does not answer the question."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Find names beginning with A, events costing between 10 and 20 inclusive, and bookings in January 2026."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Predict ",
                {
                  "tag": "code",
                  "children": [
                    "email IS NULL"
                  ]
                },
                ", ",
                {
                  "tag": "code",
                  "children": [
                    "email = 'x'"
                  ]
                },
                ", and ",
                {
                  "tag": "code",
                  "children": [
                    "NOT(email = 'x')"
                  ]
                },
                " for a NULL email."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Show the two most expensive events with deterministic ordering for ties."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Raise event 101’s fee by 5 within a transaction; compare before, during, and after ROLLBACK."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Insert a student whose name contains an apostrophe. Explain SQL escaping now and parameter binding later."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Write a DELETE that targets exactly one booking; test inside a rolled-back transaction."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Explain why rows have no guaranteed display order without ORDER BY."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "strong",
              "children": [
                "Submit:"
              ]
            },
            " SQL, predicted and actual outputs, a four-row constraint log, and corrections. ",
            {
              "tag": "strong",
              "children": [
                "Stretch:"
              ]
            },
            " design tests that distinguish empty string from NULL and missing row from a row containing NULL."
          ]
        },
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    "\n"
  ]
}
